is under threat of capture on the next move. Q: What is checkmate in chess? A: Checkmate is a condition in chess where a player's king is in a position to be captured (in 'check') and there is no way to move the king out of capture (mate). Q: What is a stalemate in chess? A: Stalemate is a situation in chess where the player whose turn it is to move is not in check but has no legal move. Q: What is castling in chess? A: Castling is a special move in chess involving the king and one of the rooks. Q: What is en passant in chess? A: En passant is a special pawn capture move in chess. Q: What is promotion in chess? A: Promotion is a chess rule that requires a pawn that reaches its eighth rank to be immediately replaced by the player's choice of a queen, knight, rook, or bishop of the same color. Q: What is the objective of chess?"}], 'model': 'telkom-ai-instruct', 'temperature': 0.5}}
